  "title": "Glacier Foundry Settlements",
  "rules": [
    "Every settler has an action row and a miner, fuelwright, mason or scout tool. Co-occupancy is allowed.",
    "Attach carried stone at the hoist while another settler holds its separate brake. Release while suspended drops the actual load and blocks its cell.",
    "Delivery creates a supported path. Eight heated ticks at the commissioned hoist turn its foundation into workshop shelter.",
    "Heat cells warm their cell and melt ice. Water flows south, erodes supports and harms exposed settlers. Shelter rest restores health.",
    "Build and heat at your feet. Scouts carry, place and recover physical markers; inventory handoffs require an adjacent waiting recipient.",
    "Use only the selected role radius-three view. Hidden map cells/entities/events stay hidden; full-state debug is separate."
  ],
